at. Retrieved April 17, 2016.","url":"https://technet.microsoft.com/en-us/library/bb490947.aspx"}]}]},{"id":"S1091","name":"Pacu","page":"tools/S1091/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--72db9534-3ac3-46df-b8ca-220727d9deb9","description":"Once inside a Virtual Private Cloud, Pacu can attempt to identify DirectConnect, VPN, or VPC Peering.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1091","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Rhino Security Labs. (2019, August 22). Pacu. Retrieved October 17, 2019.","url":"https://github.com/RhinoSecurityLabs/pacu"}]}]},{"id":"S0378","name":"PoshC2","page":"tools/S0378/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--209075a3-e836-4894-b931-663bb785e96b","description":"PoshC2 contains an implementation of netstat to enumerate TCP and UDP connections.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0378","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Nettitude. (2018, July 23). Python Server for PoshC2. Retrieved April 23, 2019.","url":"https://github.com/nettitude/PoshC2_Python"}]}]},{"id":"S0192","name":"Pupy","page":"tools/S0192/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--eb3a838e-f6dd-4e9b-8edf-fc652adde117","description":"Pupy has a built-in utility command for netstat, can do net session through PowerView, and has an interactive shell which can be used to discover additional information.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0192","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Nicolas Verdier. (n.d.). Retrieved January 29, 2018.","url":"https://github.com/n1nj4sec/pupy"}]}]},{"id":"S0445","name":"ShimRatReporter","page":"tools/S0445/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evide